      "title": "Self-RAG",
      "summary": "RAG that decides whether to retrieve, grades what it finds, checks its own answer, and retries when it is weak.",
      "url": "https://github.com/vaibhav-barman/self-rag",
      "featured": true,
      "showcase": "flagship",
      "category": "rag",
      "tags": [
        "LangGraph",
        "LangChain",
        "Groq",
        "Ollama",
        "ChromaDB",
        "Pydantic",
        "Streamlit"
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "Four reflection checks, each a Pydantic schema through Groq structured output: retrieve, ISREL (relevance), ISSUP (support) and ISUSE (usefulness).",
        "Bounded loops: at most 2 revisions and 2 rewrites, so the graph always terminates.",
        "Honest fallback: returns the best answer found with a \"limited context\" note, or says it could not find it in the documents.",
        "Each call tries the primary Groq model first, then a fallback model."
      ],
